  "overview": {
    "title": "Wild edge of the Rif coast",
    "p1": "Cap des Trois Fourches is a long, sparsely built peninsula of cliffs and open Mediterranean light — a different world from the lagoon city.",
    "p2": "Come for scenery and the feeling of space, not for services. Roads can be slow; start early and carry water and food.",
    "p3": "It is one of the strongest nature days you can take from Nador when weather and road conditions cooperate."
